WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
A reliable worker starts with a clear queue contract.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Name the owner, the lease, and the acknowledgement boundary.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Write those facts down before code begins.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
An idempotency key makes a replay safe to inspect.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Persist the key with the durable effect.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
A second attempt should observe the first result.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Heartbeats make ownership visible while work is open.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Shutdown should stop claims and preserve open attempts.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Recovery can then reconcile what the worker actually finished.
